    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst Desteği \u003e Yazılım \u0026 Özellikler",
    "content": "Bu makale, Swing Catalyst \u0026 Motion Catalyst’in 10.1 versiyonuyla tanıtılan kuvvet vektörleri özelliğinin bir uzantısı olan basınç dağılımı video overlay işlevini göstermeyi amaçlamaktadır.\nUygulanabilir yazılım varyantları: Motion Catalyst \u0026 Swing Catalyst.\nVersiyonlar: 10.2\nGerekli donanım: Denge Platformu veya Motion Plate (veya çift Motion Plate).\nWhich version of the software am I using?\nFor more details on force vectors please see our force vectors article.\nEnabling the Pressure Distribution Bar’s Just like force vectors, the pressure distribution bars require calibration.\nPlease note that there is a difference between performing a calibration in capture mode and in playback mode. If performed in capture it applies to all subsequent recordings. If performed in playback it applies only to that specific recording, therefore we recommend calibrating in capture mode so all new recordings automatically have the calibration set.\nFrom the options it’s possible to change the transparency and the colors of the pressure distribution bars.\nThis is very similar to the existing functionality for force vectors.\nPerforming a new calibration Make sure you are in capture mode if you wish for the calibration to be stored for new recordings.\nClick “Data Visuals” \u0026 “Set markers!”.\nWith the mouse click on each corner of your Balance Plate or Motion Plate / Dual Motion Plate.\nSave the calibration.\nClick “Data Visuals” again, and turn “Pressure Distribution” to “ON”.\nNote the video below is for demonstration purposes. You should select the corners of your plate in the video image.\nLast updated: 2023-12-19 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Kuvvet vektörleri gibi, basınç dağılımı çubukları da kalibrasyonu gerektirir.",
